  <scopecontent id="67cd8dcf717f262bd64433e7a0bbe283">
    <head>Scope and Contents</head>
<p>This small collection of Greer Williams's papers primarily concerns reactions to his article on "Quality versus Quantity in American Medical Education," which appeared in Science 153, no. 3739 (1966 August 26). Other materials consist of a draft of Williams's article on the Rockefeller Foundation, a book proposal, and various research notes. Apart from a few notes, most of these materials are unrelated to Williams's work on the RF's International Health Division (IHD).</p><p>Rockefeller Foundation staff separated these materials from the much larger collection of Williams's notes and manuscripts relating to the history of the IHD, which are found in the RF's Program and Policy records, SG 3.1, series 908.</p>  </scopecontent>
  <relatedmaterial id="c0b8b42a7ecf94a3cfeb36b6fa7553ee">
    <head>Related Materials</head>
<p>Greer Williams's correspondence, notes, and manuscripts relating to his consultancy for the RF and his history of the International Health Board are found in the Rockefeller Foundation records, Program and Policy SG 3.1, series 908 International Health Board, under "History."</p>  </relatedmaterial>
